Subject: flash: bflb: flash_bflb_is_valid_range must live in RAM

Every erase/write op calls flash_bflb_is_valid_range, but unlike the
rest of the op path it is not __ramfunc. Normally harmless (it runs
before the XIP suspension), but when the flash region being rewritten
CONTAINS the driver itself (OTA rewriting the running image), the op
loop calls it after its backing flash content has changed -> the CPU
fetches a half-overwritten instruction stream and faults (observed:
K_ERR_CPU_EXCEPTION at 0xa00d3e56 ~868 KB into a whole-image rewrite).

diff --git a/drivers/flash/flash_bflb.c b/drivers/flash/flash_bflb.c
--- a/drivers/flash/flash_bflb.c
+++ b/drivers/flash/flash_bflb.c
@@ -231,7 +231,8 @@
 }
 
 /* Are we doing something that makes sense? ? */
-static int flash_bflb_is_valid_range(struct flash_bflb_bank_data *data, off_t offset, size_t len)
+static __ramfunc int flash_bflb_is_valid_range(struct flash_bflb_bank_data *data, off_t offset,
+					       size_t len)
 {
 	if (offset < 0) {
 		LOG_WRN("0x%lx: before start of flash", (long)offset);
